            Beta customers brought a wish list. The biggest shift wasn't any single feature. It was
            grounding every campaign in the real threats Sublime already saw in each customer's inbox.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>A smarter builder.</strong> Templates were now built from attacks found in the
            customer's own environment. The top of the template list showed what Sublime had seen in the
            last month, like password resets, new employee onboarding, and invoice requests, and
            suggested building a campaign around them. Analysts could also stagger sends, so employees
            couldn't warn each other at the water cooler, and target Google Workspace or Microsoft 365
